      },
      "rev_n_1_98fc3e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_98fc3e_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_98fc3e",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach was flawed because it only considered the endpoints of segments and assumed that applying one segment from each set would always maximize the difference. This approach missed the potential for more optimal solutions by considering all possible combinations of segments. A better strategy would be to use a greedy approach that considers the impact of each segment on the overall range of the array, rather than just focusing on the endpoints.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_98fc3e_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_fa19908fb8",
        "created_at": 1794514797.6309829
      },
      "rev_n_2_562d21_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_562d21_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_562d21",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1: The current approach of sorting segments by length and applying them greedily is incorrect. Instead, we should consider all possible subsets of segments and calculate the effect of applying each subset. This ensures we find the optimal solution, but it's computationally expensive for large m. We can optimize by using dynamic programming to consider all subsets efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_562d21_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e02f9a0164",
        "created_at": 1794514824.7976365
      },
      "rev_n_3_4c4908_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_4c4908_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_4c4908",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1: Strategy 3: Binary search with greedy validation\n\nThis approach is more suitable for the given problem. Instead of trying to apply segments one by one, we can use binary search to find the maximum possible difference. For each potential difference, we can greedily validate if it's possible to achieve it by applying a subset of segments. This allows us to consider all possible combinations of segments efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_4c4908_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_837be178dd",
        "created_at": 1794514853.703339
      },
      "rev_n_4_c59074_0": {
